<title>USA: Middlebury, Ind., schools repriced, yields lowered.</title>
<headline>Middlebury, Ind., schools repriced, yields lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A.G. Edwards &amp; Sons, Inc. said Wednesday it repriced Middlebury Elementary School Building Corporation's $14 million bond deal, lowering yields in several maturities while leaving the top yield unchanged at 5.95 percent in 2018.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>MIDDLEBURY ELEMENTARY SCHOOL BUILDING CORPORATION</p>
<p>RE: $13,500,000</p>
<p>(ELKHART COUNTY, INDIANA) FIRST MORTGAGE REVENUE</p>
<p>BONDS, SERIES 1997</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>MOODY'S: NAF		   S&amp;P: AAA / A	     FITCH: AAA</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 04/15/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 01/15/1998</p>
<p>DUE: 01/15 &amp; 07/15</p>
<p>MATURITY		AMOUNT    AMOUNT    COUPON     PRICE</p>
<p>			   (1/15)    (7/15)</p>
